# Mobile (Expo) environment — copy to .env and fill in real values.
# Do NOT commit the real .env (it is gitignored).
#
# EVERY EXPO_PUBLIC_* VALUE IS PUBLIC. It is inlined into the JavaScript bundle
# that ships to every device and can be read out of the app binary. Never put a
# credential, API key, or secret behind an EXPO_PUBLIC_ name. There are no
# secrets in this file — all four values below are public URLs by design.
#
# Production builds validate these at startup and FAIL if any is missing, is a
# placeholder, is not https://, or points at localhost / a private LAN address
# (see lib/config.ts). Development is permissive: only the API URL is required,
# and plain http:// to your LAN IP is expected there.

# ── Required ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Backend base URL.
#   Development: your machine's LAN IP, e.g. http://192.168.1.42:8000
#   Production:  the deployed HTTPS origin, e.g. https://landhere-api.onrender.com
EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://localhost:8000

# ── Required for production builds only ───────────────────────────────────────
# App Review rejects apps without a reachable privacy policy. All three are
# linked from the Settings (Profile) screen.

EXPO_PUBLIC_PRIVACY_POLICY_URL=
EXPO_PUBLIC_TERMS_URL=
EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPPORT_URL=

# ── Removed ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# EXPO_PUBLIC_UNSPLASH_KEY no longer exists. Image lookup moved server-side
# (backend .env: UNSPLASH_ACCESS_KEY) precisely because an EXPO_PUBLIC_ key is
# shipped to every device. If that line is still in your local .env, delete it —
# and rotate the key, since any build made while it existed carried it.
